<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<resources>

  <!-- AND-12 (#334): Android 12+ IGNORES the windowBackground splash layout that
       MainTheme.Base carries (values/styles.xml) and shows the SYSTEM splash instead,
       which without these attrs is the system default: BLACK under a dark OS theme.
       This v31 override keeps the whole MainTheme.Base inheritance and only brands
       the system splash: brand splash blue background (= the csproj MauiSplashScreen
       color, dead config on Android because MainActivity declares @style/MainTheme,
       not the MAUI splash theme).
       * L18-era update (L16, Damir 2026-08-31): the ground is now #175595, his blue.
       * L16, and this REVERSES the judgment this comment used to carry. It said the
       launcher-icon default "reads correctly". It does not: with NO
       windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon declared, Android 12+ falls back to the app
       LAUNCHER icon, and the launcher icon brings its own BACKGROUND LAYER, which the
       system paints inside the splash mask. That is the squircle behind the mark that
       Damir photographed - "on light OS mode when splash is blue, remove the small logo
       background". The DARK theme never had it, because values-night-v31 supplies its own
       drawable, and the two screenshots differ for exactly that reason.
       The fix is the missing line: declare our own mark. The 140x283 @drawable/splash
       lockup the old comment worried about is NOT what is declared here - that bitmap
       belongs to the pre-31 layout and is untouched.
       Pre-31 devices never read THIS FOLDER. ⚠ They do read layout/splash_screen.xml —
       and so does every other Android, because values/styles.xml sets windowBackground
       to it with no version qualifier. An earlier draft of this row called that file
       "the pre-31 splash" and left it blue; the review caught it. Its gradient moved to
       #175595 with this one, so there is ONE blue. Out of scope, as Damir ruled: the
       @drawable/splash BITMAP that layout draws on top — a different asset. -->
  <style name="MainTheme" parent="MainTheme.Base">
    <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">#175595</item>
    <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/spixi_splash_icon</item>
    <!-- The declared mark is STATIC, and deliberately so. #336 round-2 reverted an
         ANIMATED icon on three counts (Damir F5: barely noticeable, mark too big and
         clipped by the splash circle, dots too fast). Only the second of those is about
         the mark itself, and L16 answers it: this drawable is the same white logomark the
         dark theme has shown since #534, now at ~42% of the viewport instead of ~52%,
         well inside the Android-12 66% safe circle. Nothing moves, so nothing can be
         "too fast". drawable/spixi_splash_{logo,anim}.xml stay parked for a future
         motion round. -->
  </style>

</resources>
